Chapter 1. Admin Guide

1. Overview

   This module provides a high performance database connector to interact with 
   Tarantool 3.x in-memory database using the binary IProto protocol.

   It provides asynchronous connection pooling, auto-reconnect, configurable
   failover parameters, and native KEMI exports for executing stored procedures
   and evaluating Lua code directly from SIP routing scripts.

2. Dependencies

2.1. Kamailio Modules

   The following modules must be loaded before this module:
     * none.

2.2. External Libraries or Applications

   The following libraries or applications must be installed before running
   Kamailio with this module loaded:
     * none (uses built-in zero-dependency IProto binary client with MessagePack).

3. Parameters

3.1. server (str)

   Specifies the connection URL string to the Tarantool server.
   Format: "addr=127.0.0.1;port=3301;user=rtpe_user;pass=secret;pool=4".

   Example 1.1. Set server parameter
...
modparam("ndb_tarantool", "server", "addr=127.0.0.1;port=3301;user=guest;pass=;pool=8")
...

3.2. host (str)

   Tarantool server IP address or hostname. Default is "127.0.0.1".

3.3. port (int)

   Tarantool server IProto TCP port. Default is 3301.

3.4. user (str)

   Username for authentication. Default is NULL (guest).

3.5. pass (str)

   Password for authentication. Default is NULL.

3.6. pool_size (int)

   Number of connections in the connection pool per process. Default is 4.

3.7. connect_timeout (int)

   Socket connection timeout in milliseconds. Default is 1000.

3.8. cmd_timeout (int)

   Socket I/O command timeout in milliseconds. Default is 500.

3.9. disable_time (int)

   Number of seconds communication with Tarantool is disabled after exceeding
   allowed timeouts. Default is 10.

3.10. allowed_timeouts (int)

   Number of consecutive timeouts before marking connection disabled. Default is 3.

3.11. init_without_tarantool (int)

   If set to 1, Kamailio starts successfully even if the Tarantool server is
   temporarily offline at bootstrap. Default is 0.

4. KEMI Exports

4.1. KSR.tarantool.call(proc_name, params)

   Executes a stored procedure in Tarantool 3.x via IProto protocol.

   Example 1.2. KEMI Lua Example
...
local res = KSR.tarantool.call("rtpe_select_node", "[]");
KSR.info("Selected node from Tarantool: " .. tostring(res));
...

4.2. KSR.tarantool.eval(lua_code, params)

   Evaluates an arbitrary Lua code snippet directly in Tarantool 3.x.

   Example 1.3. KEMI Python Example
...
res = KSR.tarantool.eval("return box.space.rtpe_calls:count()", "[]")
KSR.info("Active calls: %s" % res)
...
